    "own_line": true,
    "norm": "Exercises {@link StringSubstitutor#replaceIn(StringBuilder)} with the default \"${...}\" variable syntax over a buffer that contains both an escaped variable marker (\"$${\") and a complete variable reference (\"${}\"). <p>The buffer is assembled with chained {@code append(...)} calls. Each call returns the same underlying {@link StringBuilder}, so they all mutate one object — the final {@code append} copies the buffer's own current contents onto its end. Note that a {@code new char[5]} is filled with the NUL character ('\u0000'), so four NULs precede the '$'.</p>"
